\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 1. Executive Summary\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Kairo is a promising modular-monolith ERP foundation with genuinely thoughtful accounting, inventory, workflow, and multi-tenant intent. However, it is not safe for enterprise deployment today.\
The primary blocker is systemic tenant isolation failure: many endpoints authorize a supplied company context, then read or mutate records only by global ID. A user authorized in Company A can potentially target a known Company B document and cause cross-tenant disclosure or accounting/inventory corruption. The settings and master-data APIs are even less protected: they are authenticated but explicitly lack authorization.\
Facts below are repository-backed; scalability conclusions are inferences. Production behaviour under load is 
\f0\b insufficient evidence
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

